Parity reproduced EXACTLY from the web source (not a "corrected" version):
  • WINDOW_SECS: 5m=300 15m=900 1h=3600 6h=21600 24h=86400 ; BUCKET_SECS: 30s=30 1m=60 5m=300 15m=900 1h=3600.
  • Bucket option disabled  ⇔  BUCKET_SECS[b] >= WINDOW_SECS[window]  (the server "bucket >= window" 400 guard).
  • Vehicle label precedence: display_name || vin || "Vehicle {id}" (JS-falsy on empty strings). The numeric
    fallback — a bare template literal in the web — is routed through admin.xray.controls.vehicleFallback so
    native carries no English literal while rendering the identical "Vehicle 5".
  • Leading "Select vehicle…" prompt option (value nil); window/bucket option labels fall back to the raw
    literal ("5m"…) exactly like the web t(`admin.xray.windowOption.${w}`, w).
  • Page useState defaults reproduced as model defaults: vehicleId=nil, window='1h', bucket='1m'.
  Note: like the web, selecting a window that makes the current bucket invalid does NOT auto-correct the
  bucket — the now-invalid option is merely disabled in the dropdown.

